							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left"><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">  We&#039;ve been trying to catch Coir for a couple weeks now to do him again so we can move forward. UoP needed Coir just as much as IL did </div><br />Bullshit.  You guys wiped on Coirnav last weekend. You guys have had a zillion chances, and apparently have blown all of them except one.  Coirnav isn&#039;t UoP&#039;s God Given Spawn.  <br /><br />Really the problem has been more that OA has suddenly decided to bypass Arbiter and Xegony and has gone after Coirnav like 5 out of the last 7 spawns.  It really has very little to do with either UoP or IL.  <br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote"> you have to fight for kills in this game you cant expect other guilds to step out of your way and give you free attempts at mobs </div><br />That quotation is from a UoP member, right?  Why is it that when other guilds complain about wanting a chance at Coirnav, you guys say crap like that, but when others do fight for a kill, you complain?  Fighting for kills is a 2 way street, UoP.  <br /><br />I want to emphasize that we attempted to play nice and wait out all of yall&#039;s attempts and backflags, but we got sick of waiting, as mostly OA wiped over and over and over.  It became apparent that neither guild was interested in giving us a shot at him.  Our guild has been chomping at the bit to get into Time for many weeks now.  So we took matters into our own hands.  If we hadn&#039;t, who knows how many more OA and UoP wipes we would have had to wait out before Coirnav was left unmolested for IL to attempt?  It would have been another month.  Sorry, we just aren&#039;t interested in waiting that long.  <br /><br />One more little factoid I would like to bring to light:  our officers contacted UoP officers about joining forces to kill Coirnav, but UoP refused.  UoP was also asked to allow IL to allow one of its members to come along on their recent Rathe Council kill, but was refused.  It would have been very simple to trade a few flags between the two guilds.  You guys could have gotten a few Coirnav flags, we could have gotten (one I believe) a flag for Rathe Council.  IL has never been a flag hog.   We have often allowed a few stragglers to come along on our raids just to pick up a flag.  It&#039;s simply not our fault that you guys have members that still need the flag.  It&#039;s UoP&#039;s.</td>
